SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Jennifer L. Owen v. Town and Country Federal 
 Credit Union
DESCRIPTION:MAINE SUPREME JUDICIAL COURT      Reporter of Decisions \nDeci
 sion:  2026 ME 105 \nDocket:   BCD-23-442 \nArgued:   September 11\, 2024 
 \nDecided:  November 3\, 2026 \n \nPanel:  STANFILL\, C.J.\, and MEAD\, LA
 WRENCE\, DOUGLAS\, JJ.\, and HUMPHREY\, A.R.J. \n \n \nJENNIFER L. OWEN \n
  \nv. \n \nTOWN AND COUNTRY FEDERAL CREDIT UNION \n \nDOUGLAS\, J. \n[¶1]
   Jennifer L. Owen appeals from a judgment entered in the Business \nand C
 onsumer Docket (Duddy\, J.) after a jury trial in favor of Town and Countr
 y \nFederal Credit Union on her claims alleging disability discrimination 
 and \nretaliation.  Owen contends that the court abused its discretion by 
 (1) ordering \nher to pay attorney fees and costs as a discovery sanction\
 , and (2) excluding \nevidence of other former employees’ discrimination
  claims against Town and \nCountry.  We affirm the judgment. \n 2 \nI.  BA
 CKGROUND \nA. Owen’s Employment by Town and Country \n[¶2]  The followi
 ng facts are drawn from competent evidence admitted \nat trial\, viewed in
  the light most favorable to the jury’s verdict in favor of Town \nand C
 ountry.  See Sullivan v. Porter\, 2004 ME 134\, ¶ 12\, 861 A.2d 625.   \n
 [¶3]  Town and Country hired Owen as a teller in 2012.  The following \ny
 ear\, Owen was diagnosed with breast cancer.  Owen remained employed with 
 \nTown and Country and received support from her employer during her \ntre
 atment and recovery.  Town and Country and its employees organized a bake 
 \nsale\, a yard sale\, and other events to raise money to help her pay her
  medical \nexpenses.  Town and Country allowed other employees to donate p
 aid time off \nto Owen during her treatment.  By early 2014\, Owen was can
 cer-free.   \n[¶4]  In 2015\, Owen was promoted to the position of assist
 ant branch \nmanager in one of Town and Country’s South Portland branche
 s.  In this \nposition\, Owen was entrusted with managerial responsibiliti
 es in addition to \nworking with members on loans.   \n[¶5]  During the e
 nsuing year\, Owen’s performance in the assistant \nmanager position was
  unsatisfactory.  Al\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcourt/202
 6/26me105.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/sjc/lawcourt/2026/26me105.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
